{%- doc -%}
  Renders a single text node at one of ../design-system/src/react/Text/Text.tsx's roles and colour
  variants. Extracted from blocks/mionas-text.liquid so that block is not the only way to spend the
  role vocabulary: blocks/mionas-price.liquid and blocks/mionas-product-description.liquid render
  their dynamic product copy through here instead of restating --text-role-* by hand, which is how
  they drifted out of step with the roles in the first place.

  THE .text-role CSS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT LIVE HERE. Snippets cannot declare a stylesheet tag,
  and it stays in blocks/mionas-text.liquid, which is where it already was. Every block
  stylesheet tag is compiled into one file that ships on every page -- verified byte-identical
  across the home page, /cart and a collection page -- so a caller does not need mionas-text to be
  present on the page for these classes to resolve.

  CALLERS MUST SANITISE `content` THEMSELVES. This snippet outputs it unfiltered, because
  mionas-text passes richtext that has already been flattened to inline HTML and the product blocks
  pass values from `| money` and product.title. Nothing here escapes; nothing here strips tags.

  @param {string} content - The text to render. Emitted unfiltered; see above.
  @param {string} [role] - A Text.tsx role: hero, title, subtitle, heading, subheading, caption, lead, body, label, stamp. Defaults to body.
  @param {string} [variant] - A colour variant: default, primary, inverse-primary, inverse-primary-muted, accent, accent-inverse, tint. Defaults to default.
  @param {string} [tag] - p, span, div or h1-h6. Anything else falls back to p.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes for the caller's own box (padding, weight overrides).
  @param {string} [heading_level] - When set, emits role="heading" aria-level="<n>" instead of a real <h*>, matching snippets/text.liquid's product-title branch.
  @param {string} [shopify_attributes] - The caller's block.shopify_attributes, so the theme editor can still select the block.

  @example
  {% render 'mionas-text', content: product.title, role: 'body', tag: 'p', class: 'mionas-price' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign resolved_role = role | default: 'body'
  assign resolved_variant = variant | default: 'default'

  comment
    tag comes from a select in every caller today, but a snippet is reachable from anywhere, so an
    unknown value falls back to p rather than emitting an invalid element.
  endcomment
  assign allowed_tags = 'p|span|div|h1|h2|h3|h4|h5|h6' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_tag = tag | default: 'p'
  unless allowed_tags contains resolved_tag
    assign resolved_tag = 'p'
  endunless

  assign classes = 'text-role text-role--' | append: resolved_role | append: ' text-role--' | append: resolved_variant
  if class != blank
    assign classes = classes | append: ' ' | append: class
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The tag is interpolated rather than switched through a {% case %}. blocks/mionas-text.liquid
  carried a ten-branch case for this, one per allowed tag, differing only in the element name; with
  the value whitelisted above there is nothing left for the branches to guard.
{%- endcomment -%}
<{{ resolved_tag }}
  class="{{ classes }}"
  {%- if heading_level != blank %}
    role="heading"
    aria-level="{{ heading_level }}"
  {%- endif %}
  {{ shopify_attributes }}
>{{- content -}}</{{ resolved_tag }}>
